# Human-readable colour palette for Inky Frame Spectra 7.3.
# Generated by `convert <image> -unique-colors -format PNM -compress none palette.pnm`
# To view palette, you can use `convert palette.pnm -scale 1000% palette.png`
# To use the palette to generate a nicely-dithered bmp, use:
#   `convert <image-in> -ordered-dither h4x4o -remap palette.pnm <image-out>.bmp` (Ordered, has a bit of a pattern)
#   or `convert <image-in> -dither Floyd-Steinberg -remap palette.pnm <image-out>.bmp` (Disordered, but can have some artefacts)
